title: CatConvoDay2
position: 647,285
---
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
    <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
<<else>>
    <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
<<endif>>
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
<<if $playerKnowsHowGnarpTalks == false>>
    <<set $playerKnowsHowGnarpTalks = true>>
    {$catName}: I want tell you something. About how I learn your words.
    {$catName}: I listen. I repeat. I break sound into parts. Your ship leak many tiny noise: logs, error words, old training tapes.
    {$catName}: I practice alone. I want be understood, not just... heard.
<<endif>>
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: First time I talk, I was new. Now I more... independent.
{$catName}: I can stay longer. I can keep my fear quiet.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: You sleep many day. I thought you gone. Then you move again. I send more messages to your ship.
    -> Why did you leave last time?
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: Last time I talk with you, I leave because I must.
        {$catName}: My planet... not really like humans.
        {$catName}: Talking to you is dangerous for me.
            -> Dangerous how?
                <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        {$catName}: Sorry. I want tell you. I can't.
        -> It's okay. Sorry.
            <<positive_indicator Cat>>
            <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
            <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
            {$catName}: Thank you.
        -> But why? What's happening on your planet?
            <<negative_indicator Cat>>
            <<set $catDislikesYou += 1>>
            <<show_character Cat Angry right>>
            {$catName}: Stop. Please.
            <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
            {$catName}: I really not allowed.
            <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        -> ...
{$catName}: But enough about scary thing. I want know about you!
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: What is like being human? What you do all day in metal box?
{$catName}: I find word in your ship log... "breakfast"? You eat first thing when wake up?
{$catName}: We not do that on my planet. Morning is for listening. You sit and hear what world tell you.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: But I like idea. Start day with something nice for yourself. What your breakfast like?
    -> Er, protein paste... from a tube.
        <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
        {$catName}: Paste! From tube! Like... medicine? You eat medicine for breakfast?
        {$catName}: That is maybe saddest thing I ever hear. But also little bit funny. Sorry.
    -> Um... I try not to think about it.
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        {$catName}: So bad you block from memory. I understand. Some thing deserve forgetting.
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: Oh! And your ship make sound. Constant sound. Low and steady. Like... breathing?
{$catName}: I think at first it was music. I listen for long time trying to find the pattern.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: Then I realize... no pattern. Just machine. But still... I like it. It feel alive.
<<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
{$catName}: I try hum your ship sound once. Match the tone. It was... comforting? Like sitting next to something warm.
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
The signal holds steady. {$catName} is still there, waiting patiently on the other side.
    -> (keep talking)
        <<jump CatConvoDay2_Part2>>
    -> (end the conversation)
        <<jump CatConvoDay2_End>>
===

title: CatConvoDay2_Part2
position: 647,400
---
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<positive_indicator Cat>>
<<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: It nice talking to you. You make silence less heavy.
    -> So, what do you actually... do?
<<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
{$catName}: Fun! Yes! I was hoping you ask.
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: Everyone on my planet is so... busy. Always working. Always serious. Rules and watching and duties.
{$catName}: I not understand. Life is already short. Why spend all of it being boring?
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: So I play. I make up game. I solve puzzle. I draw in my journal.
{$catName}: Puzzle is my favorite. Pattern make world feel less random.
<<if $catLikesYou >= $catDislikesYou>>
    <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
    {$catName}: You want try? I have puzzle!
    <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
    <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
    I let {$catName} beam a simple puzzle to my device, with shapes, colors, and repeating sequences.
    It shouldn't feel intimate... but somehow, it does anyway.
    <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
    {$catName} falters on patterns that should be easy, like the translator is eating pieces of the rules.
        -> (win at the game)
            <<positive_indicator Cat>>
            <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
            <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
            <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
            {$catName}: You good. Teach me? I want learn from you.
        -> (purposefully lose the game)
            <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
            <<positive_indicator Cat>>
            <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
            <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
            {$catName}: I win! I win!
            {$catName}: Maybe someday I teach you. I practice a lot.
<<endif>>
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
The signal holds steady. {$catName} is still there, waiting patiently on the other side.
    -> (keep talking)
        <<jump CatConvoDay2_Part3>>
    -> (end the conversation)
        <<jump CatConvoDay2_End>>
===

title: CatConvoDay2_Part3
position: 647,515
---
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
{$catName}: Can I tell you something? About... my family?
{$catName}: They still on planet. They not gone or anything. But... they distant.
{$catName}: My mom and dad, they work for security group. Important people. They protect planet, make big decision.
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: They always busy. Always watching for threat. Not have much time for me.
{$catName}: It strange. Right here. But feel far away.
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
    <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
    <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
    {$catName}'s voice dips.
        -> Is everything okay?
            <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
            {$catName}: I fine. Just... remembering.
            <<positive_indicator Cat>>
            <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
            {$catName}: Big trouble would happen if mom or dad found out about you.
            <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
            {$catName}: Talking to you help. You make space less sharp.
            <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
            {$catName}: I very lucky to have you here.
            <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
            Making someone feel less alone... brings me a quiet warmth.
<<else>>
    <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
    <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
    {$catName} goes quiet. The silhouette holds still.
        -> ...
<<endif>>
<<if $catLikesYou >= $catDislikesYou>>
    <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
        -> So what do you do while your family is off being important?
            <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
            <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
            {$catName}: Oh! I... I have job too, actually. Not important like theirs. But still job.
            {$catName}: I watch space. Monitor for anything that come close. And I have to write about it. Keep record of everything I see. Every day, same thing. Nothing happen, but I still write it down.
    {$catName}: Sometimes I wonder if anyone even read what I send. Maybe it just go into big pile somewhere and disappear.
    <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
    {$catName}: So most of the time... I draw instead.
    {$catName}: In my journal. Little pictures. Stars, nebula, your ship one time. I draw what I see and what I imagine.
    <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
    {$catName}: My favorite is the one with rings near your star. I draw it so many time the page is almost full.
    <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
    <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
    I think about my own reports. Status updates, every few months, the same nothing typed up and sent to people who probably don't read it. 
    I take the work seriously... someone has to. But the idea of doodling stars in the margins instead is oddly charming.
        -> I wish I had that freedom. My reports are pretty strict.
            <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
            <<positive_indicator Cat>>
            <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
            <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
            {$catName}: Strict? No drawing allowed? That sound terrible!
            {$catName}: Maybe I send you one of mine sometime. So you have something nice to look at between all the boring word.
            <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        -> I get bored too. But I just push through it.
            <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
            <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
            {$catName}: Push through... that sound very human. All work, no drawing.
            <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
            {$catName}: Maybe that why you need someone like me. To remind you that boredom is just creativity with nowhere to go.
    I didn't expect to find common ground over paperwork. But here we are.
    <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
    The conversation thins to nothing, and for a while neither of us speaks. Just the hum of my ship and whatever distant sound lives on theirs.
    <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
    <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
    {$catName}: ...This is nice.
    <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
    {$catName}: The quiet. With you. It feel different than quiet alone.
    {$catName}: Alone quiet is... empty. This quiet is... full?
    <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
    {$catName}: I don't mind waiting. For you to talk, for you to wake up. I don't mind it.
    {$catName}: Just knowing you there is enough.
    <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
<<endif>>
And then, without either of us deciding to, the conversation just... keeps going.
<<fade_transition 1.5>>
<<wait 1>>
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: ...and the color is not blue, not green. No word in your language. It is like... if cold had a color but was warm?
    -> ...
<<fade_transition 1.5>>
<<wait 1>>
<<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
{$catName}: ...wait, you only have ONE mouth? How you eat and talk at same time?
    -> ...
<<fade_transition 1.5>>
<<wait 1>>
<<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
{$catName}: ...no no no, you say it wrong! The joke is the animal fall UP, not down! That is why it funny!
    -> ...
<<fade_transition 1.5>>
<<wait 1>>
<<show_character Cat Sad right>>
{$catName}: ...sometimes the quiet get so big I forget what my own voice sound like. Then I talk to you and I remember.
    -> ...
<<fade_transition 1.5>>
<<wait 1>>
<<show_character Cat Happy right>>
{$catName}: ...okay okay, one more question. If you could bring ONE thing from your planet, not big thing, small thing, what would you bring?
    -> ...
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
<<fade_transition 1.5>>
<<wait 1>>
I glance at the mission clock and the number doesn't make sense. I check it again.
Over an hour. We've been talking for over an hour.
I look back at the screen. {$catName} is mid-thought, leaning forward, completely at ease. Like the static and the distance and the impossibility of all of this is just... background noise now.
When was the last time I lost track of time with someone? I honestly can't remember.
Everything about {$catName} is new. Every answer opens a door I didn't know existed. It's the kind of conversation where you never run out of things to ask because you haven't asked anything yet.
<<jump CatConvoDay2_End>>
===

title: CatConvoDay2_End
position: 647,630
---
<<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
My mind shifts back to the report I need to write. 
<<if $posSelfPerception > $negSelfPerception>>
    I decide to end the conversation for now. It's been a while since I've talked with somebody new.
<<else>>
    I feel my social battery start to drain, so I decide to end the conversation for now.
<<endif>>
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
    <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
    {$catName}: Already? This was good. Really good.
    <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
    {$catName}: But okay. I understand.
    {$catName}: Next time we talk... I have more thing to tell you. Many more.
    <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
    I believe that. Right now, it feels like we could talk forever and never hit the bottom.
    I wonder if that's true, or if it's just what new feels like.
<<else>>
    <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
    {$catName}: Okay. I go.
    <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
    The screen lingers for a moment before the feed cuts. I notice I don't feel the pull to keep talking the way I did at the start.
<<endif>>
<<jump AfterCatLeavesDay2>>
===

title: AfterCatLeavesDay2
position: 915,224
---
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<play_music MainTheme>>
The silhouette shudders, then collapses back into static.
<<hide MonitorSilhouette>>
<<show MonitorOn>>
Silence rushes in like a pressure change.
My reflection looks wrong on the dark glass, like someone who knows something they shouldn't.
HQ's reminder sits in my inbox, timestamped weeks ago, delivered while I was asleep.
"Remember your duty to report accurately. Your observations are crucial for our understanding and eradication of foreign threats."
    -> (report {$catName})
        If I send this, HQ will know. And their protocol for "foreign threats" doesn't involve follow-up conversations.
        I think about {$catName}'s voice. The puzzles. The silence that felt full.
        The word "eradication" stares back at me from the inbox.
            -> (report {$catName} anyway)
                <<jump WriteReportDay2_Report>>
            -> (do not report)
                <<jump WriteReportDay2_DontReport>>
    -> (do not report)
        <<jump WriteReportDay2_DontReport>>
